commit 7f51be219e4d21669b72388838e19adb663c3180

C03: File Explorer launches verify by a new CabinetWClass window of the shell; openings of known software absent from the catalog become a presence read (APPS1233 repair)

Provider: the shell's Explorer entry is observed through its CabinetWClass
windows (the shell process also owns the desktop and taskbar) and a window
absent from the pre-launch baseline identifies the launch even when its
process pre-existed (APPS1231/005, /006: verification_failed while the window
was on screen). Mind: «abrime el photoshop», «abri photoshop», «no, mejor abrí
firefox», «Abrime Lightroom.» read as app.installed on the literal name when
the verified catalog has no such entry, instead of a model guess that denied
the capability or asked for the exact name (APPS1231/007–009, /015, /016);
«abrí la puerta» stays outside, and with no catalog nothing changes. Offline
recogniser baseline unchanged. No tests (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


